---

## Highlights

- **Zero Console Clutter**: Native Win32 GUI entrypoint with `NUL` IO redirection—no black terminal windows.
- **Strict Process Supervision**: Windows Job Object binding ensures all `node.exe` processes terminate when the PWA closes—**zero zombie processes, instant port 3080 release**.
- **Direct Node.js Bypass**: Auto-detects global `npm` / `pnpm` / `yarn` modules to bypass shell startup latency (cascades to `pwsh` → `powershell` → `cmd` if needed).
- **0% CPU Idle**: Win32 `SetWinEventHook` + `MsgWaitForMultipleObjects` sleep until the window closes—**zero polling, zero CPU overhead**.

---

## Quick Start

### 1. Prerequisites
- Global DSH: `npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh` or `pnpm add -g @deepseek-ai/dsh`
- Edge PWA: Open `http://127.0.0.1:3080/` in Edge and click "Install App" in the address bar.

### 2. Create Shortcuts
Download and extract the [Latest Release](https://github.com/2bitbit/dsh-desktop/releases/latest), then run in PowerShell:

```powershell
# Interactive Mode: pops up a folder picker to choose your workspace
.\install_shortcut.ps1

# CLI Mode: specify the target directory directly
.\install_shortcut.ps1 -TargetDirectory "D:\Your\Workspace"
```
> 💡 **Equivalent Command**: Clicking the created shortcut is **equivalent to executing `dsh web --no-open` in that directory and automatically launching/managing the Edge PWA window**.

---

## Architecture

```
Shortcut (--cwd <dir>) ──> dsh_pwa_shim.exe ──(Job Object)──> Node.js (dsh web)
                                │
                                ├─ 30ms TCP probe on port 3080
                                ├─ Launch Edge PWA & capture HWND/PID
                                └─ Sleep (0% CPU) ──[Close Window]──> Instant Job tree teardown
```

---

## CLI Options

| Option | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `--cwd <path>` / `-w <path>` | Set DSH working directory (equivalent to running `dsh web` inside it) | `dsh_pwa_shim.exe --cwd "D:\Projects\Demo"` |
| `--debug` / `-d` | Enable debug logging & dialogs | `dsh_pwa_shim.exe --debug` |

---

## Build from Source

```powershell
.\scripts\build.ps1
```

